# Kept out of the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies config, middleware, models, routes, services and
# server.js by name, so none of this was ever in the image - but the whole
# context is uploaded to the daemon before the first instruction runs, and
# ml/.venv alone is 370MB. The image installs its own dependencies from the
# lockfile, so a host-built node_modules would also mix binaries from a
# different platform into an Alpine image.
node_modules
ml
tests
data
.git
.env
.env.*
*.log
npm-debug.log*
